window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-035.json",{"day":35,"title":"When a Museum Receives a Difficult Gift","targetWords":[{"word":"detect","gloss":"查明","context":"Her job was to detect restrictions that could complicate the museum's work long after the opening photographs had appeared in the newspapers.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"weigh","gloss":"权衡","context":"The offer seemed generous, but the director had to weigh obligations before accepting it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"remark","gloss":"话语","context":"An early remark in the donor's letter suggested a scheme to control the exhibition.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"scheme","gloss":"图谋","context":"An early remark in the donor's letter suggested a scheme to control the exhibition.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"accomplish","gloss":"完成","context":"They could accomplish more by explaining uncertainty than by trying to assure everyone that no problem existed.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"assure","gloss":"向……保证","context":"They could accomplish more by explaining uncertainty than by trying to assure everyone that no problem existed.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"dismiss","gloss":"忽视","context":"The curator did not presume bad faith, yet she refused to dismiss the concern.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"govern","gloss":"支配","context":"She would contemplate compromise, but not one that allowed a private sponsor to govern historical conclusions.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hesitate","gloss":"犹豫","context":"Staff should not have to shrug at pressure or hesitate to raise concerns.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"conceive","gloss":"设想","context":"They should not plot an emotionally manipulative route through the rooms or conceive of visitors as passive recipients.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"plot","gloss":"策划","context":"They should not plot an emotionally manipulative route through the rooms or conceive of visitors as passive recipients.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"contend","gloss":"主张","context":"The donor could object to a label, contend that criticism was unfair, or argue that gratitude should prevent public disagreement.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"deem","gloss":"认为","context":"The museum would deem the display successful if people learned how interpretations were formed, even when they did not all reach the same conclusion.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"devise","gloss":"设计","context":"The team began to ask questions and devise a transparent assessment process.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"digest","gloss":"消化","context":"They would inspect objects, digest documents, and report what the records could indicate.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"manifest","gloss":"体现","context":"An old toy could evoke curiosity, while a military portrait might manifest a family's ideas about authority.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"comprehend","gloss":"领悟","context":"Curators needed to comprehend provenance rather than simply tell an attractive tale.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"contemplate","gloss":"考虑","context":"She would contemplate compromise, but not one that allowed a private sponsor to govern historical conclusions.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":{"en":"contemplate a change","zh":"认真考虑改变"}},{"word":"entail","gloss":"涉及","context":"A careful investigation would entail expense, but avoiding that cost might eventually harm both the museum's reputation and the public's understanding of the past.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"worship","gloss":"崇拜","context":"A museum director was asked to receive a collection from a wealthy donor who hoped the institution would worship his family's achievements.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"evoke","gloss":"唤起","context":"An old toy could evoke curiosity, while a military portrait might manifest a family's ideas about authority.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"shrug","gloss":"耸肩","context":"Staff should not have to shrug at pressure or hesitate to raise concerns.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"intrude","gloss":"干预","context":"They needed to know that professional duties would protect them when an influential person might intrude into decisions that properly belonged to the institution.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"avert","gloss":"避免","context":"Staff would be able to return an object if its ownership proved unlawful and avert misleading claims before publication.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"presume","gloss":"假定","context":"The curator did not presume bad faith, yet she refused to dismiss the concern.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"complicate","gloss":"使复杂","context":"Her job was to detect restrictions that could complicate the museum's work long after the opening photographs had appeared in the newspapers.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"retrospect","gloss":"回顾","context":"In retrospect, the director believed the most important agreement concerned what would happen when disagreement returned.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"answer","gloss":"回答","context":"Instead, learners could exercise judgment, talk about alternatives, and answer questions using the material available.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"ask","gloss":"问","context":"The team began to ask questions and devise a transparent assessment process.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"report","gloss":"报告","context":"They would inspect objects, digest documents, and report what the records could indicate.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"talk","gloss":"说","context":"Instead, learners could exercise judgment, talk about alternatives, and answer questions using the material available.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"require","gloss":"需要","context":"Would the gift support public learning, or require the museum to conceal uncomfortable history?","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"tell","gloss":"告诉","context":"Curators needed to comprehend provenance rather than simply tell an attractive tale.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"teach","gloss":"教","context":"The education team also discussed how the collection would teach younger visitors.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"support","gloss":"支持","context":"Would the gift support public learning, or require the museum to conceal uncomfortable history?","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"control","gloss":"控制","context":"An early remark in the donor's letter suggested a scheme to control the exhibition.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"order","gloss":"顺序","context":"A contract could rule out unreasonable interference and set the order in which disputed issues were considered.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"rule","gloss":"排除","context":"A contract could rule out unreasonable interference and set the order in which disputed issues were considered.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"receive","gloss":"收到","context":"A museum director was asked to receive a collection from a wealthy donor who hoped the institution would worship his family's achievements.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"challenge","gloss":"挑战","context":"A damaged painting might fit the collection's main theme, while a forged signature could challenge its entire story.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"explain","gloss":"解释","context":"Teachers would explain why an object's meaning changes when placed beside new evidence.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"return","gloss":"归还","context":"Staff would be able to return an object if its ownership proved unlawful and avert misleading claims before publication.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"protect","gloss":"保护","context":"They needed to know that professional duties would protect them when an influential person might intrude into decisions that properly belonged to the institution.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"argue","gloss":"论述","context":"The donor could object to a label, contend that criticism was unfair, or argue that gratitude should prevent public disagreement.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"relate","gloss":"联系","context":"The director tried to relate each disputed decision to the museum's mission.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"prevent","gloss":"阻止","context":"The donor could object to a label, contend that criticism was unfair, or argue that gratitude should prevent public disagreement.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"exercise","gloss":"练习","context":"Instead, learners could exercise judgment, talk about alternatives, and answer questions using the material available.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"fit","gloss":"符合","context":"A damaged painting might fit the collection's main theme, while a forged signature could challenge its entire story.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"indicate","gloss":"表明","context":"They would inspect objects, digest documents, and report what the records could indicate.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"object","gloss":"反对","context":"The donor could object to a label, contend that criticism was unfair, or argue that gratitude should prevent public disagreement.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"A museum director was asked to receive a collection from a wealthy donor who hoped the institution would worship his family's achievements. The offer seemed generous, but the director had to weigh obligations before accepting it. Would the gift support public learning, or require the museum to conceal uncomfortable history? An early remark in the donor's letter suggested a scheme to control the exhibition. The curator did not presume bad faith, yet she refused to dismiss the concern. Her job was to detect restrictions that could complicate the museum's work long after the opening photographs had appeared in the newspapers.","zh":"一位富裕捐赠者邀请博物馆馆长接收藏品，希望机构崇拜其家族成就。提议看似慷慨，馆长却必须先权衡责任。礼物会支持公共学习，还是要求隐瞒不舒服的历史？捐赠信早先的一句话暗示了控制展览的图谋。馆长没有预先认定恶意，也不愿忽视疑虑。她的职责是发现限制，它们可能在开幕照登报很久之后，仍使工作复杂化。"},{"en":"The team began to ask questions and devise a transparent assessment process. They would inspect objects, digest documents, and report what the records could indicate. A damaged painting might fit the collection's main theme, while a forged signature could challenge its entire story. Curators needed to comprehend provenance rather than simply tell an attractive tale. They could accomplish more by explaining uncertainty than by trying to assure everyone that no problem existed. A careful investigation would entail expense, but avoiding that cost might eventually harm both the museum's reputation and the public's understanding of the past.","zh":"团队开始提问，设计透明评估流程。他们检查物件、消化档案、报告记录所能表明的内容。受损画作可能符合藏品主题，伪造签名却可能挑战整个故事。策展人需要理解来源，而非仅讲好听故事。解释不确定性比保证没问题更有价值。认真调查涉及费用，但回避成本最终可能损害博物馆声誉和公众对过去的理解。"},{"en":"Negotiations required tact. The donor could object to a label, contend that criticism was unfair, or argue that gratitude should prevent public disagreement. The director tried to relate each disputed decision to the museum's mission. She would contemplate compromise, but not one that allowed a private sponsor to govern historical conclusions. A contract could rule out unreasonable interference and set the order in which disputed issues were considered. Staff should not have to shrug at pressure or hesitate to raise concerns. They needed to know that professional duties would protect them when an influential person might intrude into decisions that properly belonged to the institution.","zh":"谈判需要技巧。捐赠者可能反对标签、认为批评不公平，或说感激应阻止公开分歧。馆长把每个争议决定与使命联系起来。她会考虑妥协，但不会允许私人赞助者支配历史结论。合同可排除不合理干预、规定处理争议的顺序。员工不应无奈耸肩或迟疑于提出疑虑，而应知道，当有影响力的人侵入本属于机构的决定时，职业责任会保护他们。"},{"en":"The education team also discussed how the collection would teach younger visitors. An old toy could evoke curiosity, while a military portrait might manifest a family's ideas about authority. Teachers would explain why an object's meaning changes when placed beside new evidence. They should not plot an emotionally manipulative route through the rooms or conceive of visitors as passive recipients. Instead, learners could exercise judgment, talk about alternatives, and answer questions using the material available. The museum would deem the display successful if people learned how interpretations were formed, even when they did not all reach the same conclusion.","zh":"教育团队讨论如何用藏品教年轻游客。旧玩具能唤起好奇，军人画像可能体现家族对权威的观念。教师解释物件为何在新证据旁改变意义。他们不应策划操纵情绪的路线，也不应把游客设想为被动接受者。学习者可以练习判断、讨论替代解释、用现有材料回答问题。只要人们学会解释如何形成，即使结论不同，博物馆也会认为展览成功。"},{"en":"In retrospect, the director believed the most important agreement concerned what would happen when disagreement returned. Staff would be able to return an object if its ownership proved unlawful and avert misleading claims before publication. The museum could not promise to please every supporter, but it could promise to explain its choices. The donor eventually accepted these limits, recognizing that credibility would give his collection lasting value. A gift becomes genuinely public when its recipient remains free to examine it. Without that freedom, a museum risks becoming a handsome room where money decides which questions visitors are permitted to consider.","zh":"回顾时，馆长认为最重要的协议是规定分歧再现时怎么办。若所有权证明违法，员工可以归还物件；出版前也能避免误导说法。博物馆无法承诺讨好每个支持者，却能解释选择。捐赠者最终接受限制，认识到可信度给藏品带来长期价值。接受者仍可自由审视时，礼物才真正属于公众。失去这种自由，博物馆可能只是漂亮房间，由金钱决定游客获准考虑哪些问题。"}],"previous":34,"next":36});
